<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Rail offers fall on soft demand.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Rail offers fall on soft demand.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rail basis offers for spot soymeal fell Wednesday, under pressure from rising CBOT prices and soft demand in domestic and export markets, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Once you have meal up around $300.00 (per ton), people are going to start looking for other sources (of feed), a river dealer said.</p>
<p>With the recent strength in CBOT prices, flat soymeal offers have climbed to and above $300.00 per ton in some areas, brokers said.</p>
<p>That historically high price has discouraged end-users from buying much soymeal, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soymeal merchandisers are also expecting another high crush on Thursday, despite the market's steep prices, they said.  </p>
